# Workspace-local toolchains and downloaded artifacts
/.tools/

# Common local output
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.dmp
*.wav
# ...except the one setup embeds. The engine smoke test compares a whole
# transcript against pinned ground truth, so the clip has to travel with the
# code that asserts on it. The previous fixture was gitignored, lived only in
# `.tools/`, and by 2026-08-18 had been lost from every checkout on this
# machine -- taking the proof with it. `scripts/New-SmokeFixture.ps1`
# regenerates this one from Windows' own synthesiser.
!apps/bootstrapper/fixtures/smoke.wav

# That exception is the ONLY one, and it is a synthesised clip on purpose.
#
# `crates/speakeasy-audio/examples/record_fixture.rs` records real speech from a
# real microphone, and those recordings are a person's voice. They stay on the
# machine that made them: this is a public repository, and a voice is not a
# fixture you can un-publish. `.tools/` already covers them and `*.wav` covers
# them again -- both deliberately, so removing one does not expose them.
#
# **Do not add a second `!` exception for a recorded clip.** If a proof needs
# real speech, it needs the recorder and a local recording, not a committed
# voice. That is the standing decision (owner, 2026-08-27) and it is why the
# recorder is committed while its output never is.

# Production workspace output
/target/
/artifacts/streaming-qualification/
/artifacts/transcribe-cpp-benchmark/
